(a) The parks and recreation board, when established, shall consist of seven appointed members, serving without pay. Five members shall be appointed by the county, one member shall be appointed by the city of Camilla, and one member shall be appointed by the city of Pelham for initial terms, as provided in subsection (b) of this section. The replacement terms of office for the members of the parks and recreation board shall be for five years or until their successors are appointed and qualified. Each member may be reappointed.
(b) In order that the term of at least one member shall expire annually, the original appointments shall be made by the parties as follows:
(1) The county, by and through its board of commissioners, shall appoint one member who resides in the geographical boundaries that coincide with Commissioner District 1 for the board of commissioners, for an initial term of five years;
(2) The county, by and through its board of commissioners, shall appoint one member who resides in the geographical boundaries that coincide with Commissioner District 2 for the board of commissioners, for an initial term of four years;
(3) The county, by and through its board of commissioners, shall appoint one member who resides in the geographical boundaries that coincide with Commissioner District 3 for the board of commissioners, for an initial term of three years;
(4) The county, by and through its board of commissioners, shall appoint one member who resides in the geographical boundaries that coincide with Commissioner District 4 for the board of commissioners, for an initial term of two years;
(5) The county, by and through its board of commissioners, shall appoint one member who resides in the geographical boundaries that coincide with Commissioner District 5 for the board of commissioners, for an initial term of one year;
(6) The City of Camilla, by and through its mayor and council, shall appoint one member for an initial term of one year; and
(7) The City of Pelham, by and through its mayor and council, shall appoint one member for an initial term of one year.
Upon the expiration of each initial term, replacement member positions on the parks and recreation board shall be each shall be appointed in the same manner as the initial appointments were made, for a five-year term.
(c) All members of the parks and recreation board may be reimbursed for actual expense incurred in connection with their official duties.
(d) Any vacancy on the parks and recreation board shall be filled for the unexpired term by the governing body whose appointee vacates the position.
(e) Each governing body shall have complete authority to remove its appointed member(s) of the parks and recreation board for cause. Cause for removal includes, but is not limited to, a member's absence from three consecutive parks and recreation board meetings without just cause.
(Ord. No. 2019-006, § 1(Exh. A), 12-10-2019)

